Ansible Basics for Beginners 🐧

Today I played with two simple Ansible Playbooks – perfect for anyone starting in DevOps:

✅ Apache HTTPD Install Playbook – Automates the installation & service start of Apache HTTP server in seconds.
 ✅ Create User Playbook – Easily creates and manages users across multiple servers.

🔹 What is a Playbook?
 A playbook is like a blueprint for automation. It’s written in YAML and contains a list of tasks that Ansible will execute step-by-step on your servers.

🔹 Why Playbooks?
 ✅ Automate repetitive tasks
 ✅ Maintain consistency across multiple servers
 ✅ Human-readable format
 ✅ Reusable and version-controlled

💡 Shortcut Tip:
  In Playbooks :
🔹name → Description of task
🔹hosts → Target group name from inventory
🔹become: yes → Root permissions
🔹Modules like yum, service, user → Action type
